        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "title": "Read me",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Qwen-Image 2.1 + Fun ControlNet Union + Tiled Diffusion\n\nA tiled refine of an image under a structure ControlNet. Load any image (the *Load Image* node), it is scaled to ~3 MP (16-multiples), a Canny edge map is taken from it, and Qwen 2.1 re-renders it at **denoise 0.6** with the Fun ControlNet Union holding the edges, through Tiled Diffusion (Mixture of Diffusers, 1408 px tiles, 384 overlap).\n\n**What Tiled Diffusion does for the Fun ControlNet (since 2026-10-21):** the control image is encoded **once at full canvas** and each tile gets **its own crop**. Before that, ComfyUI's Fun ControlNet patch resized the whole control image to whatever latent it was called with, so under tiling every tile got the entire edge map squashed into it and the picture tore into fragments. Tiled Diffusion also forces `tile_batch_size` to 1 while Fun ControlNets are present (the patch holds one control image per model call).\n\n**ControlNet window:** ComfyUI's `start_percent` / `end_percent` are on the model's *whole* schedule, not on the denoise window. To have the ControlNet on for a fraction of *your run*, use `percent = (1 - denoise) + run_fraction x denoise`. Here: on from 2% to 70% of a denoise-0.6 run = start **0.412**, end **0.82**. (At end_percent 0.5 and a low denoise the ControlNet would never fire.) The model card trains the adapter at strength 1.0; lower it if it fights the picture.\n\n**Files (Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1):** `diffusion_models/qwen_image_2.1_*.safetensors`, `text_encoders/qwen3vl_8b_*.safetensors`, `vae/qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors`, `model_patches/qwen_image_2.1_fun_controlnet_union_*.safetensors` (alibaba-pai; 8 condition types in one file: canny, depth, grayscale, HED, lineart, MLSD, pose, scribble; the type is read from the image itself).\n\nSeveral *Apply Fun ControlNet* nodes can be chained (each with its own image, strength and window); Tiled Diffusion crops every one of them per tile.\n"
      ]
    }
